WEBVTT

00:00:07.625 --> 00:00:11.167
Makise Kurisu...!

00:00:11.167 --> 00:00:13.208
I tried knocking, but...

00:00:13.208 --> 00:00:15.208
H-How did you find this place?

00:00:15.208 --> 00:00:17.167
I asked Hashida-<i>san</i>.

00:00:17.167 --> 00:00:21.125
He called it a laboratory, so
I expected something a little more proper--

00:00:21.125 --> 00:00:23.292
Daru! Did you betray me?!

00:00:23.292 --> 00:00:24.417
Huh?

00:00:24.417 --> 00:00:27.208
You were taken in by this 3D girl's spell!

00:00:27.208 --> 00:00:31.458
You'll pay for this! Indeed, you shall!

00:00:31.458 --> 00:00:34.000
You bitch!

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:36.083
Could you do something about him?

00:00:36.083 --> 00:00:38.958
Just think of it as situational confusion.

00:00:38.958 --> 00:00:40.958
Emergency situation.

00:00:40.958 --> 00:00:44.250
The Organization has
finally sent an agent here.

00:00:44.250 --> 00:00:47.833
What?! This is the
choice of Steins Gate as well?!

00:00:47.833 --> 00:00:49.083
Steins Gate...?

00:00:49.083 --> 00:00:52.833
One of his neurotic fantasies.
It doesn't really mean anything.

00:00:52.833 --> 00:00:57.125
Hardly surprising. It's a
jumble of German <i>and </i>English.

00:00:57.125 --> 00:00:59.625
No shoes.

00:00:59.625 --> 00:01:01.417
Oh, I'm sorry!

00:01:01.417 --> 00:01:03.708
I was in America for so long...

00:01:05.958 --> 00:01:09.250
Allow me to reintroduce
myself. I'm Makise Kurisu.

00:01:11.083 --> 00:01:16.625
You can't even shake my hand?
Japanese men have no sense of etiquette.

00:01:19.417 --> 00:01:21.958
You're acting <i>too </i>afraid.

00:01:21.958 --> 00:01:25.000
Yes, it must be the aura
of bloodlust surrounding you.

00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:28.250
Is this what they call "martial arts"?

00:01:30.625 --> 00:01:31.833
Where are you going?!

00:01:31.833 --> 00:01:36.042
Actually, I came to see if you
really had witnessed me being stabbed

00:01:36.042 --> 00:01:42.000
or if it was just an excuse
for sexually harassing me.

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:43.583
But more importantly...

00:01:57.708 --> 00:02:02.917
<i>For you, billions and billions of heartbeats</i>

00:02:02.917 --> 00:02:09.583
<i>are nothing at all; just the blink of an eye</i>

00:02:09.583 --> 00:02:14.792
<i>Although I'm trapped by</i>
<i>the past and lament the future</i>

00:02:14.792 --> 00:02:20.708
<i>inevitability won't allow for</i>
<i>even a speck of a miscalculation</i>

00:02:20.708 --> 00:02:26.833
<i>Our dreams and futures that</i>
<i>form and expand into "infinity"</i>

00:02:26.833 --> 00:02:32.667
<i>allow us the right to be vain,</i>

00:02:32.667 --> 00:02:38.917
<i>while the two hands</i>
<i>point out what is "finite"</i>

00:02:38.917 --> 00:02:43.500
<i>All of which leads to a cruel</i>
<i>contract and choice to make</i>

00:02:43.500 --> 00:02:45.750
<i>Hacking to the Gate</i>

00:02:45.750 --> 00:02:52.667
<i>So, now, with each passing</i>
<i>second, I'll cross world lines</i>

00:02:52.667 --> 00:02:57.583
<i>to protect that smile on your face</i>

00:02:57.583 --> 00:03:04.583
<i>Then, once again, into a</i>
<i>time loop without sadness</i>

00:03:04.583 --> 00:03:11.250
<i>I will be swallowed up as a lone observer</i>

00:03:29.167 --> 00:03:31.250
Their attachment site is undamaged.

00:03:31.250 --> 00:03:33.583
There's no trickery involved.

00:03:33.583 --> 00:03:36.333
She may be planning to plant explosives.

00:03:36.333 --> 00:03:37.792
Keep a sharp eye on her.

00:03:37.792 --> 00:03:39.500
Get real...

00:03:39.500 --> 00:03:40.750
--Have any tweezers?
--No.

00:03:40.750 --> 00:03:42.542
Okay.

00:03:42.542 --> 00:03:44.500
The inside's squishy.

00:03:44.500 --> 00:03:46.167
It tastes like...

00:03:46.167 --> 00:03:47.958
Nothing. Yuck!

00:03:47.958 --> 00:03:51.333
You vile zombie! If you're hungry, just say so!

00:03:51.333 --> 00:03:52.667
I can give you a banana!

00:03:52.667 --> 00:03:56.583
No thanks. Who'd eat a
pervert's banana anyway?

00:03:56.583 --> 00:03:57.625
Pervert?!

00:03:57.625 --> 00:04:00.792
You started poking and groping
me the moment you met me.

00:04:00.792 --> 00:04:03.500
--Miss Makise, Miss Makise.
--Yes?

00:04:03.500 --> 00:04:08.500
Could you say, "Who'd eat a
pervert's banana anyway?" again?

00:04:08.500 --> 00:04:10.583
With a distressed look, if possible.

00:04:10.583 --> 00:04:13.625
--Distressed?
--Yeah.

00:04:13.625 --> 00:04:17.333
What are you blushing for?
Oh, did you imagine something?

00:04:17.333 --> 00:04:21.833
Tell us, genius girl! What did
your gifted mind just envision?

00:04:21.833 --> 00:04:24.958
Please, do tell!

00:04:24.958 --> 00:04:27.750
It would appear that you're <i>both </i>perverts.

00:04:27.750 --> 00:04:29.375
--You're too kind...
--That's not praise.

00:04:29.375 --> 00:04:32.750
I'd say the one with the
perverted imagination is the pervert...

00:04:32.750 --> 00:04:34.750
Perverted genius girl!

00:04:34.750 --> 00:04:36.500
Who are you calling a pervert?!

00:04:36.500 --> 00:04:38.333
Okay, I'll be frank.

00:04:38.333 --> 00:04:40.875
I could easily sue you for
sexual harassment this very minute,

00:04:40.875 --> 00:04:42.375
but I'll overlook it for now.

00:04:42.375 --> 00:04:43.417
For now?

00:04:43.417 --> 00:04:45.667
So give me the details.

00:04:45.667 --> 00:04:49.042
This banana has something to
do with that microwave, correct?

00:04:49.042 --> 00:04:50.583
That's top-secret!

00:04:50.583 --> 00:04:53.667
Future Gadget #8, the Phone
Microwave (Temporary Name),

00:04:53.667 --> 00:04:56.708
is our laboratory's secret weapon.

00:04:58.167 --> 00:05:02.875
Actually, if anyone, Miss Makise might
be able to explain this crazy functionality.

00:05:02.875 --> 00:05:03.875
But...

00:05:03.875 --> 00:05:08.042
Seriously, we're never
gonna figure it out on our own.

00:05:08.042 --> 00:05:11.833
But this is classified
Future Gadget Laboratory--

00:05:15.500 --> 00:05:18.125
You! Christina, you said?

00:05:18.125 --> 00:05:19.458
I never said that.

00:05:19.458 --> 00:05:21.500
I'll tell you the secrets of the
Phone Microwave (Temporary Name),

00:05:21.500 --> 00:05:23.833
but only on certain conditions!

00:05:23.833 --> 00:05:30.167
First, you must become a member
of the Future Gadget Laboratory.

00:05:30.167 --> 00:05:33.750
So you want me to join your lab?

00:05:34.292 --> 00:05:38.958
But I'm returning to America in August.

00:05:38.958 --> 00:05:40.833
Until then, then.

00:05:40.833 --> 00:05:42.958
--Second...
--There's more?

00:05:42.958 --> 00:05:48.042
You must forget about <i>all</i>
sexual harassment I have committed.

00:05:48.042 --> 00:05:49.083
Those are my conditions!

00:05:49.083 --> 00:05:53.125
You're petty, Okarin. Seriously petty...

00:05:53.125 --> 00:05:55.875
That's what I love about ya!

00:05:55.875 --> 00:05:57.000
Shut up!

00:05:57.000 --> 00:06:01.250
--So? A good deal, wouldn't you say?
--For <i>you</i>, maybe.

00:06:01.250 --> 00:06:04.708
Sheesh. You're causing me
to secrete excess noradrenaline.

00:06:04.708 --> 00:06:07.042
What do you say, Christina?

00:06:07.042 --> 00:06:08.750
Don't call me that!

00:06:08.750 --> 00:06:10.917
My bad, The Zombie!

00:06:10.917 --> 00:06:13.708
Say it right, Hououin Pervert Kyouma!

00:06:13.708 --> 00:06:17.000
Be quiet, pervert genius girl!

00:06:17.000 --> 00:06:19.500
Two perverts staring
each other down! That's hot!

00:06:19.500 --> 00:06:20.958
Shut up, pervert!

00:06:20.958 --> 00:06:24.542
Oh, all right. Fine. I accept.

00:06:24.542 --> 00:06:29.042
Just quit with the "pervert" stuff.
I'll quit treating you like one too.

00:06:29.042 --> 00:06:30.292
Very well.

00:06:30.292 --> 00:06:34.333
Then, as of now, you are
officially Lab Member 004...

00:06:34.333 --> 00:06:36.333
...Christina!

00:06:36.333 --> 00:06:37.958
And don't call me that!

00:06:37.958 --> 00:06:41.750
Juicy #1 Chicken Tenders! Wow!

00:06:41.750 --> 00:06:43.625
--I'm back!
--It's a teleporter?

00:06:43.625 --> 00:06:45.708
It's dangerous to jump
to conclusions, you know.

00:06:45.708 --> 00:06:47.250
Then what do <i>you </i>think is it?

00:06:47.250 --> 00:06:49.583
Well, it didn't teleport the chicken tenders...

00:06:49.583 --> 00:06:52.917
--...or the banana bunch, right?
--One, two, three, four...

00:06:52.917 --> 00:06:55.000
Oh? A visitor?

00:06:56.375 --> 00:06:59.667
Hello. I'm Makise Kurisu.

00:06:59.667 --> 00:07:02.167
I'm sorry for visiting unannounced.

00:07:02.167 --> 00:07:03.875
I'm Shiina Mayuri.

00:07:03.875 --> 00:07:06.958
It looks like I'm a lab member now too...

00:07:06.958 --> 00:07:09.250
--A lab member?
--Yes.

00:07:09.250 --> 00:07:12.708
A girl lab member!

00:07:12.708 --> 00:07:15.375
I-Is it that rare?

00:07:15.375 --> 00:07:17.333
Yeah, yeah, yeah!

00:07:17.333 --> 00:07:20.833
You're the first girl member besides Mayushii!

00:07:20.833 --> 00:07:22.250
Really?

00:07:22.250 --> 00:07:24.083
Nice to meetcha!

00:07:24.083 --> 00:07:26.667
--Yes! Likewise!
--What?!

00:07:26.667 --> 00:07:27.667
What is it?

00:07:27.667 --> 00:07:29.250
There was an electrical discharge!

00:07:29.250 --> 00:07:32.250
Huh? Why didn't you mention it sooner?!

00:07:32.250 --> 00:07:33.875
Give me all the details!

00:07:33.875 --> 00:07:36.375
Huh? Well, uhh...

00:07:36.375 --> 00:07:39.125
Lightning-ish stuff came
outta the microwave, and...

00:07:39.125 --> 00:07:42.625
--When was this?
--Yesterday, around noon.

00:07:42.625 --> 00:07:46.750
You'd rushed out after seeing
the news about the satellite crash,

00:07:46.750 --> 00:07:49.333
so I hooked my own cell phone up to it.

00:07:52.542 --> 00:07:55.042
So, wait, when I sent that e-mail,

00:07:55.042 --> 00:07:58.750
your phone was connected to the
Phone Microwave (Temporary Name)?

00:07:58.750 --> 00:08:01.792
The e-mail about Miss Makise getting stabbed?

00:08:01.792 --> 00:08:03.292
That was last week, man.

00:08:03.292 --> 00:08:06.625
No! I sent it at noon yesterday--!

00:08:08.000 --> 00:08:10.625
Where is it?! Where is it?! Why isn't it here?!

00:08:10.625 --> 00:08:13.375
What was the microwave doing
when the discharge occurred?

00:08:13.375 --> 00:08:15.208
I was doing an operations test,

00:08:15.208 --> 00:08:18.083
so I think it was spinning
in reverse at the time.

00:08:18.083 --> 00:08:20.375
Sounds like we should try to recreate it.

00:08:20.375 --> 00:08:23.375
Mayuri! Bring the Juicy #1 Chicken Tenders!

00:08:23.375 --> 00:08:24.458
Okay!

00:08:24.458 --> 00:08:27.875
Oh, do you all want some?
You can each have one!

00:08:27.875 --> 00:08:29.375
Does something need to be inside?

00:08:29.375 --> 00:08:31.875
I want to see what happens to an object inside

00:08:31.875 --> 00:08:34.125
when it's spinning in reverse.

00:08:34.125 --> 00:08:35.750
Daru.

00:08:38.250 --> 00:08:40.542
Assistant. Send a message to my phone.

00:08:40.542 --> 00:08:43.167
Since when am I your assistant?

00:08:43.167 --> 00:08:45.625
Besides, I don't even know your e-mail address.

00:08:45.625 --> 00:08:47.458
Lousy useless assistant.

00:08:47.458 --> 00:08:49.667
Daru. Your phone will do.

00:08:49.667 --> 00:08:52.042
--What should it say?
--Hmm...

00:08:52.042 --> 00:08:53.875
"Christina is a pervert..."

00:08:53.875 --> 00:08:55.917
I told you, that's not allowed.

00:08:55.917 --> 00:09:00.542
Then I'll meet you halfway
and go with, "Okarin is a pervert."

00:09:00.542 --> 00:09:02.500
--Wha...?!
--Hashida-<i>san</i>! Good job!

00:09:02.500 --> 00:09:05.542
Okay! Gonna send it now!

00:09:05.542 --> 00:09:07.708
Now we wait for the message to arrive...

00:09:07.708 --> 00:09:11.042
They should be ready about now!

00:09:11.042 --> 00:09:12.583
Wait!

00:09:24.917 --> 00:09:27.917
--You okay?!
--Yeah...

00:09:29.167 --> 00:09:30.750
Ventilation! Ventilation!

00:09:35.417 --> 00:09:37.083
What just happened?

00:09:37.083 --> 00:09:38.958
Was it the EM waves?

00:09:38.958 --> 00:09:40.875
Don't be stupid.

00:09:40.875 --> 00:09:45.458
A microwave oven's EM waves
couldn't wreck a desk in such a short time.

00:09:45.458 --> 00:09:47.583
Ahh! They're charred black!

00:09:47.583 --> 00:09:50.167
I just bought 'em, too...

00:09:50.167 --> 00:09:51.708
What about the hole in the floor?

00:09:51.708 --> 00:09:54.917
Mr. Braun's totally gonna
freak when he sees it...

00:10:00.625 --> 00:10:02.667
--Well?
--It's here...

00:10:02.667 --> 00:10:07.042
Received July 24th, at 5:30 pm...

00:10:07.042 --> 00:10:10.333
It really did go back in time...

00:10:12.333 --> 00:10:15.833
--Have you figured something out?
--Yes! It all connects!

00:10:15.833 --> 00:10:19.875
Now I see! The one answer
that connects this string of events!

00:10:19.875 --> 00:10:21.958
Really?

00:10:21.958 --> 00:10:25.167
The banana returned to
the bunch it was torn from!

00:10:25.167 --> 00:10:27.750
And this e-mail traveled
five days into the past!

00:10:27.750 --> 00:10:29.750
No, you don't mean...

00:10:29.750 --> 00:10:31.292
Indeed, I do!

00:10:31.292 --> 00:10:33.875
This Phone Microwave (Temporary Name) is...

00:10:37.958 --> 00:10:39.792
...a time machine!

00:10:52.250 --> 00:10:55.958
Thirteen messages...?

00:10:55.958 --> 00:10:58.583
From "S. F."...

00:10:58.583 --> 00:11:02.458
Oh, right. That girl I named "Shining Finger."

00:11:02.458 --> 00:11:05.542
Man, look at all these...

00:11:05.542 --> 00:11:06.917
"E-mail me right away."

00:11:06.917 --> 00:11:08.833
"Are you asleep?"

00:11:08.833 --> 00:11:11.458
"How long are you gonna sleep?"

00:11:11.458 --> 00:11:13.083
Daru...

00:11:16.083 --> 00:11:18.250
Wanna go for a walk?

00:11:19.500 --> 00:11:22.167
--What's wrong?
--Critical damage...

00:11:22.167 --> 00:11:24.500
We worked all through the night for nothin'...

00:11:24.500 --> 00:11:26.875
I regret even trying.

00:11:26.875 --> 00:11:30.042
Why aren't they turning
into gel-nanas anymore?

00:11:31.917 --> 00:11:33.500
Beats me.

00:11:33.500 --> 00:11:36.333
That was the only time we
managed to send an e-mail, too.

00:11:36.333 --> 00:11:39.542
Maybe we should ask Miss Makise back here?

00:11:39.542 --> 00:11:41.708
You know that's not gonna happen.

00:11:41.708 --> 00:11:45.542
No way... A time machine...?!

00:11:47.958 --> 00:11:50.125
And then she never came back.

00:11:50.125 --> 00:11:53.083
What was her deal?

00:11:53.083 --> 00:11:54.792
What's this?

00:11:54.792 --> 00:11:56.667
The LHC.

00:11:56.667 --> 00:11:57.667
Huh?

00:11:57.667 --> 00:12:01.750
The Large Hadron Collider.
SERN's particle accelerator.

00:12:01.750 --> 00:12:04.500
It's such a soothing sight...

00:12:08.292 --> 00:12:14.375
SERN maintains a strict monopoly
on the time machine market.

00:12:14.375 --> 00:12:17.125
John Titor...

00:12:17.125 --> 00:12:19.708
Oh, that guy you mentioned before?

00:12:19.708 --> 00:12:22.458
@channel's going crazy over him now.

00:12:22.458 --> 00:12:24.125
What's SERN?!

00:12:24.125 --> 00:12:29.000
Titor said that SERN
completes a time machine by 2034!

00:12:29.000 --> 00:12:30.542
You're making no sense...

00:12:30.542 --> 00:12:32.958
Just tell me! What's SERN--?!

00:12:32.958 --> 00:12:35.000
Cut it out!

00:12:35.000 --> 00:12:38.625
It's the acronym for the European
Organization in Nuclear Research.

00:12:38.625 --> 00:12:41.000
It's based just outside Geneva.

00:12:41.000 --> 00:12:44.792
As its name suggests, it focuses
mainly on particle physics research.

00:12:44.792 --> 00:12:47.458
It boasts some of the
finest facilities in the world too,

00:12:47.458 --> 00:12:50.125
including the Low Energy Antiproton Ring,

00:12:50.125 --> 00:12:52.208
the Proton Synchrotron Booster,

00:12:52.208 --> 00:12:54.250
the Large Electron-Positron Collider,

00:12:54.250 --> 00:12:56.333
and the last boss...

00:12:56.333 --> 00:13:01.583
...the world's biggest particle
accelerator: Large Hadron Collider-<i>tan</i>!

00:13:03.417 --> 00:13:10.625
There were even rumors that the
LHC could produce mini-black holes.

00:13:12.708 --> 00:13:14.417
Black holes...

00:13:14.417 --> 00:13:16.542
--Daru.
--Yeah?

00:13:16.542 --> 00:13:20.583
Doesn't one theory suggest
that time travel is possible

00:13:20.583 --> 00:13:24.125
through the use of mini-black holes?

00:13:24.125 --> 00:13:29.333
Yeah, but you heard
Miss Makise's lecture, remember?

00:13:29.333 --> 00:13:32.792
She said it's impossible to
generate black holes to begin with.

00:13:32.792 --> 00:13:36.292
But with the LHC, it's possible--

00:13:36.292 --> 00:13:38.708
Good point! Not.

00:13:38.708 --> 00:13:40.583
SERN publicly denied it.

00:13:40.583 --> 00:13:44.542
But where there's smoke there's fire.

00:13:44.542 --> 00:13:46.167
It's me.

00:13:46.167 --> 00:13:47.917
Yes. I know.

00:13:47.917 --> 00:13:50.583
El Psy Congroo.

00:13:50.583 --> 00:13:52.833
Who exactly are you battling?

00:13:52.833 --> 00:13:56.250
At this juncture, we've
but one course of action.

00:13:56.250 --> 00:13:57.833
Go visit Faris-<i>tan</i>!

00:13:57.833 --> 00:14:00.875
No! You're a super hax0r, right?!

00:14:00.875 --> 00:14:02.750
Just grin and go along with everything I say!

00:14:02.750 --> 00:14:04.875
It's "hacker," not "hax0r." Get it right.

00:14:04.875 --> 00:14:08.000
--You know your next task, right?
--Not a clue.

00:14:09.875 --> 00:14:12.625
Hack into SERN.

00:14:12.625 --> 00:14:14.500
That is all.

00:14:14.500 --> 00:14:17.417
Okarin... You're joking, right?

00:14:17.417 --> 00:14:22.417
Unveil their evildoing and
find out about their time machine.

00:14:22.417 --> 00:14:26.250
Your skills will determine whether
the Phone Microwave (Temporary Name)

00:14:26.250 --> 00:14:30.458
becomes a usable time machine or
ends up in the back of our lab's closet.

00:14:30.458 --> 00:14:32.375
Don't blame me for whatever happens!

00:14:32.375 --> 00:14:35.333
Two beef bowls. That'll be 800 yen total.

00:14:35.333 --> 00:14:37.792
Okarin!

00:14:40.167 --> 00:14:42.000
Slacking off again?

00:14:42.000 --> 00:14:43.375
Uh-huh.

00:14:43.375 --> 00:14:46.417
There's nothing to do
at the shop. It's so boring.

00:14:46.417 --> 00:14:49.375
You're more like a bicycle shop now.

00:14:49.375 --> 00:14:53.542
Say, what are you guys up to upstairs?

00:14:53.542 --> 00:14:55.833
It's called the Future Gadget Laboratory, right?

00:14:55.833 --> 00:14:57.833
H-How do you know that name?!

00:15:00.875 --> 00:15:03.708
Very well, then. If you know that much...

00:15:03.708 --> 00:15:09.042
We're battling a secret organization
that controls the world from the shadows.

00:15:09.042 --> 00:15:13.292
In fact, we're just about to
launch a hacking offensive against it.

00:15:13.292 --> 00:15:18.083
Oh, then is "SERN" that secret organization?

00:15:18.083 --> 00:15:19.167
How do you know that?!

00:15:19.167 --> 00:15:23.833
I'm sorry. I heard you guys talking up there...

00:15:23.833 --> 00:15:26.000
Like I said, it gets really boring. So I just--

00:15:26.000 --> 00:15:28.833
You were spying on us?!

00:15:28.833 --> 00:15:30.750
I can't help that I can hear you.

00:15:30.750 --> 00:15:35.000
But don't worry! I'm great at keeping secrets!

00:15:37.208 --> 00:15:37.958
Not again.

00:15:37.958 --> 00:15:40.333
What is it? A death report?

00:15:40.333 --> 00:15:41.458
A what?!

00:15:41.458 --> 00:15:44.500
O-Oh, I'm just kidding...

00:15:44.500 --> 00:15:47.250
It's just this girl with a rabid obsession

00:15:47.250 --> 00:15:49.708
with some retro PC called an IBN 5100...

00:15:49.708 --> 00:15:50.917
An IBN?

00:15:50.917 --> 00:15:53.500
You've heard of it?!

00:15:53.500 --> 00:15:55.625
Y-Yeah...

00:15:55.625 --> 00:16:00.708
--You overheard that too?
--No, no! I saw it online!

00:16:00.708 --> 00:16:05.083
You know, that time
traveler guy. John Titor, was it?

00:16:05.083 --> 00:16:06.125
Titor?!

00:16:06.125 --> 00:16:09.125
I read about it on @channel.

00:16:09.125 --> 00:16:14.500
The IBN 5100 was built
before PCs could run BASIC,

00:16:14.500 --> 00:16:18.000
so it can read IBN's proprietary
programming language or something--

00:16:18.000 --> 00:16:20.083
--Really?!
--Y-Yeah...

00:16:20.083 --> 00:16:23.917
Come to think of it, the Titor
who appeared in 2000 also said...

00:16:28.625 --> 00:16:35.167
You all seem to have fixed
views about the concept of time.

00:16:35.167 --> 00:16:41.375
Time is not like a single
river flowing from past to future.

00:16:42.542 --> 00:16:48.208
For example, let's say I go back in
time and kill someone we'll call "A."

00:16:48.208 --> 00:16:52.250
Doing so will change what is
known as the "divergence number"

00:16:52.250 --> 00:16:57.917
and the world line will
move to a world without A.

00:16:57.917 --> 00:17:02.583
When a world line moves,
people's memories are reconstructed.

00:17:02.583 --> 00:17:07.708
In other words, memories of the
world in which A existed are erased

00:17:07.708 --> 00:17:14.500
and replaced with memories of
a world line where A doesn't exist.

00:17:14.500 --> 00:17:17.042
I've been wanting to know for a while now--

00:17:17.042 --> 00:17:19.958
how exactly does SERN, a research organization,

00:17:19.958 --> 00:17:23.042
wind up as an administrative
body that rules the world?

00:17:23.042 --> 00:17:26.667
Do not take SERN's word at face value.

00:17:26.667 --> 00:17:31.833
They have already succeeded
in producing micro black holes.

00:17:31.833 --> 00:17:34.958
Perhaps the easiest way to
describe this dystopia would be to call it

00:17:34.958 --> 00:17:40.292
a revival of communism with
18th-century living standards.

00:17:40.292 --> 00:17:46.333
In 2036, SERN possesses most of
the world's science and technology.

00:17:46.333 --> 00:17:51.417
And you need an IBN 5100
to alter this future of yours?

00:17:51.417 --> 00:17:53.417
Correct.

00:17:53.417 --> 00:17:59.750
The IBN 5100's abilities are
needed to halt SERN's plans.

00:17:59.750 --> 00:18:04.542
As I recall, the John Titor who
appeared in 2000 said something similar...

00:18:04.542 --> 00:18:07.500
The "me" who appeared ten years ago?

00:18:07.500 --> 00:18:13.208
As I said before, I've unfortunately
never been to the year 2000.

00:18:13.208 --> 00:18:18.042
However, it's possible you
saw me in another world line.

00:18:18.042 --> 00:18:23.625
I'm intrigued. I'd very much
like to talk with you sometime.

00:18:23.625 --> 00:18:29.042
This is my e-mail address.
If you contact me, I'll reply.

00:18:34.250 --> 00:18:37.042
Almost there...

00:18:37.042 --> 00:18:39.167
If I can just get ahold of the SQL table list...

00:18:39.167 --> 00:18:43.333
--...grabbing the password will be a cinch.
--Too-too-roo! Good morning!

00:18:43.333 --> 00:18:45.417
Oh, Mayuri.

00:18:45.417 --> 00:18:47.167
What brings you here so early?

00:18:47.167 --> 00:18:52.292
I heard you pulled two all-nighters
in a row, so I brought some stuff!

00:18:52.292 --> 00:18:54.542
Tadah!

00:18:54.542 --> 00:18:55.833
Canned <i>oden </i>stew!

00:18:55.833 --> 00:18:58.583
Many thanks! Continue to bring more, Mayuri!

00:18:58.583 --> 00:19:04.000
Mayushii doesn't have enough
pocket money to treat you all the time.

00:19:04.000 --> 00:19:07.458
I need to buy Rai-Net sausages too, after all!

00:19:07.458 --> 00:19:08.750
More Oopas, huh?

00:19:08.750 --> 00:19:12.042
So I hope you'll savor and enjoy this!

00:19:12.042 --> 00:19:15.917
There's some for Daru-<i>kun </i>and Kurisu-<i>chan </i>too!

00:19:15.917 --> 00:19:17.708
No, not there!

00:19:17.708 --> 00:19:19.542
He doesn't hear me at all.

00:19:19.542 --> 00:19:21.583
I keep telling him to take a break.

00:19:21.583 --> 00:19:26.167
His super hax0r soul is burning brightly!

00:19:26.167 --> 00:19:28.167
It's not "hax0r"!

00:19:31.125 --> 00:19:34.375
It isn't nice to pry into
others' business, you know.

00:19:34.375 --> 00:19:36.958
It's to expose SERN's plot.

00:19:36.958 --> 00:19:38.542
Still...

00:19:38.542 --> 00:19:43.625
I think Kurisu-<i>chan </i>ran out
because she was mad about it.

00:19:43.625 --> 00:19:48.083
No, she left on her own,
not because of the hacking.

00:19:48.083 --> 00:19:51.833
I hope she'll come back...

00:19:56.000 --> 00:19:57.583
Huh? What?

00:19:57.583 --> 00:19:59.667
I'll trade a fishcake for a beef strip.

00:19:59.667 --> 00:20:02.542
Oh? Then I'd rather have a quail patty.

00:20:02.542 --> 00:20:06.208
Nope. Quail patties are my
second favorite, after beef strips.

00:20:06.208 --> 00:20:08.833
Mayushii likes them too, though.

00:20:08.833 --> 00:20:11.583
Then take a fish tube instead.

00:20:11.583 --> 00:20:15.417
--I <i>guess </i>that's better than a fishcake...
--Excellent. We have a deal.

00:20:15.417 --> 00:20:17.750
Then here's Mayushii's beef strip--

00:20:17.750 --> 00:20:19.167
--Huh?
--Already took it.

00:20:19.167 --> 00:20:22.000
Huh?! When did you...?

00:20:23.750 --> 00:20:26.208
Pretty good.

00:20:28.292 --> 00:20:31.792
Got it!

00:20:31.792 --> 00:20:34.042
I got it! I got it! I got it!

00:20:34.042 --> 00:20:38.250
Now give it up and reveal everything to me!

00:20:38.250 --> 00:20:40.958
--Yes! Got an ID!
--You're in?!

00:20:40.958 --> 00:20:43.417
Mission complete!

00:20:43.417 --> 00:20:46.667
You're amazing! Even if
I don't understand why...

00:20:46.667 --> 00:20:48.667
Well, I did hack our way in,

00:20:48.667 --> 00:20:52.500
but there's only so much we
can see without an admin ID...

00:20:52.500 --> 00:20:55.000
Like only getting to see a character's boobs!

00:20:55.000 --> 00:20:56.542
You're so naughty, Daru-<i>kun</i>.

00:20:56.542 --> 00:21:01.375
--So what did you find?!
--Just a few e-mails so far.

00:21:01.375 --> 00:21:04.292
English?! Let's consult Dr. Excite for help!

00:21:04.292 --> 00:21:07.125
Forget that! Too annoying!

00:21:07.125 --> 00:21:09.375
Translated, it says, "Hi, Paul!"

00:21:09.375 --> 00:21:12.417
--The acting is unnecessary.
--Aww.

00:21:12.417 --> 00:21:13.625
Let's see...

00:21:13.625 --> 00:21:16.042
"The LHC is working well.

00:21:16.042 --> 00:21:18.500
It's as fickle as a cat,

00:21:18.500 --> 00:21:21.542
but things have been going
surprisingly well this past month."

00:21:21.542 --> 00:21:24.208
--What does that mean?
--You got me.

00:21:24.208 --> 00:21:27.917
Never mind that! Are there
any mentions of a time machine?!

00:21:27.917 --> 00:21:31.083
The phrase "time machine" doesn't show up,

00:21:31.083 --> 00:21:35.875
but the term "Z-Program" was used
about 100 times in the past month.

00:21:35.875 --> 00:21:36.833
Let's see here...

00:21:36.833 --> 00:21:42.500
"Z-Program Experiment Report 137..."

00:21:42.500 --> 00:21:47.292
"As the aim of generating mini-black
holes has already been established,

00:21:47.292 --> 00:21:50.333
that report is omitted."

00:21:50.333 --> 00:21:51.833
Mini-black holes...

00:21:51.833 --> 00:21:52.958
Seems so!

00:21:52.958 --> 00:21:56.542
They publicly announced those
experiments were a failure, though!

00:21:56.542 --> 00:21:57.958
What's after that?!

00:21:57.958 --> 00:21:59.833
"Experimental result..."

00:22:02.667 --> 00:22:07.458
"Human is dead. Mismatch."

00:22:07.458 --> 00:22:09.833
Human is dead?

00:22:09.833 --> 00:22:11.500
Yeah...

00:22:11.500 --> 00:22:12.958
Someone...

00:22:15.000 --> 00:22:16.625
...died?

00:22:27.083 --> 00:22:35.042
<i>With my vision restricted, there's no escape</i>

00:22:36.042 --> 00:22:43.792
<i>from the merciless control of the twelve</i>

00:22:43.792 --> 00:22:52.667
<i>Wishing for a tomorrow of repose,</i>

00:22:52.667 --> 00:23:01.375
<i>I embark for the horizon of the</i>
<i>sacred phenomenon in my hand</i>

00:23:01.375 --> 00:23:10.000
<i>Trapped by the covenant and</i>
<i>shown the outline of false evidence</i>

00:23:10.000 --> 00:23:19.125
<i>the heaven and earth of</i>
<i>life lets time blindly flow by</i>

00:23:19.125 --> 00:23:28.000
<i>Flutter, butterfly, oh, miraculous</i>
<i>butterfly! I give myself to you</i>

00:23:28.000 --> 00:23:35.167
<i>Oh, butterfly of tears,</i>
<i>dazzling butterfly! It's all...</i>

00:23:35.167 --> 00:24:02.070
<i>...about to be rewritten now</i>
